"""
A bidirectional connection over a Unix domain socket.

SocketConnection objects are returned by UnixSocketServer>>accept
and UnixSocketClient>>connectTo: (unwrap their Success first). They
support both raw byte I/O and line-based protocols (ideal for JSON-RPC).

Failure contract (CONVENTIONS §1): `send:`, `sendLine:`, `receive`,
`receive:` and `receiveLine` answer a Result on both paths -- `Success`
wrapping the receiver (sends) or the received String (receives), or
`Failure` with the reason (connection closed, EOF, I/O error). A
non-Integer byte count signals.

```example
"Line-based JSON-RPC protocol"
| conn <SocketConnection> response <String> |
conn := (UnixSocketClient connectTo: '/tmp/rpc.sock') value.
conn sendLine: '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"ping","id":1}'.
response := conn receiveLine value.
conn close
```

```example
"Raw send/receive"
| conn <SocketConnection> data <String> |
conn := (UnixSocketClient connectTo: '/tmp/app.sock') value.
conn send: 'HELLO'.
data := conn receive value.
conn close
```
"""
SocketConnection subclass: Object

  """
  Send raw string data over the connection. Answers Success wrapping
  the receiver, or Failure if the connection is closed or the write fails.

  ```example
  conn send: 'hello world'
  ```
  """
  method: send: data <String> ^<Result> ! <IO> [
      ^self primSend: data
  ]

  """
  Send a string followed by a newline. Useful for line-delimited
  protocols like JSON-RPC. Answers Success wrapping the receiver, or
  Failure if the connection is closed or the write fails.

  ```example
  conn sendLine: '{"method":"test"}'
  ```
  """
  method: sendLine: data <String> ^<Result> ! <IO> [
      ^self primSendLine: data
  ]

  """
  Read up to 4096 bytes from the connection. Blocks until data
  is available. Answers Success wrapping the String read, or Failure
  on EOF, a closed connection, or an I/O error.

  ```example
  | data <String> |
  data := conn receive value
  ```
  """
  method: receive ^<Result> ! <IO> [
      ^self primReceive
  ]

  """
  Read up to maxBytes bytes from the connection. Answers Success
  wrapping the String read, or Failure (EOF, closed, I/O error). A
  non-Integer maxBytes signals.

  ```example
  | data <String> |
  data := (conn receive: 1024) value
  ```
  """
  method: receive: maxBytes <Integer> ^<Result> ! <IO> [
      ^self primReceiveMax: maxBytes
  ]

  """
  Read one newline-delimited line. The trailing newline is stripped.
  Blocks until a full line is available. Answers Success wrapping the
  line (a final unterminated line is answered as-is), or Failure on EOF,
  a closed connection, or an I/O error.

  ```example
  (conn receiveLine)
      onSuccess: [:line | line]
      onFailure: [:reason | conn close]
  ```
  """
  method: receiveLine ^<Result> ! <IO> [
      ^self primReceiveLine
  ]

  """
  Close the connection.

  ```example
  conn close.
  conn isClosed   "=> true"
  ```
  """
  method: close ! <IO> [
      ^self primClose
  ]

  """
  True if the connection has been closed.
  """
  method: isClosed ^<Boolean> [
      ^self primIsClosed
  ]
